  <running_head>MATERIA / RIARUM.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">MATE</l>
    <l n="2">2. Varii casus excepti enumerantur.</l>
    <l n="3">3. Quid moribus obtineat?</l>
    <l n="4">4. Emptor utili actione ante traditionem</l>
    <l n="5">rei experiri potest.</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Emptio recipit conditionem, quae</l>
    <l n="8">adversatur ejus substantiae.</l>
    <l n="9" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="10">1. Quae res divendi possint, vel non?</l>
    <l n="11">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="12">3. Quid si res sacra fuerit divendita?</l>
    <l n="13">4. Quid circa rerum venditiones jure He-</l>
    <l n="14">braeorum fuerit observatum?</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 3. INSTIT. TIT. 25.</l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Locatione &amp; conductione.</l>
    <l n="17" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="18">1. Locatio definitur.</l>
    <l n="19">2. Differentia inter locationem &amp;</l>
    <l n="20">emptionem traditur.</l>
    <l n="21">3. Multiplex inter utrumque contractum</l>
    <l n="22">est convenientia.</l>
    <l n="23">4. Moribus in locatione praediorum instru-</l>
    <l n="24">mentum requiritur.</l>
    <l n="25">5. Effectus locationis enumerantur.</l>
    <l n="26">6. Quid in conductione operis obtineat?</l>
    <l n="27">7. Quinam sint effectus conductionis?</l>
    <l n="28">8. Moribus conductor qui est in mora non</l>
    <l n="29">tenetur ad usuras.</l>
    <l n="30" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="31">1. Explicatur casus singularis.</l>
    <l n="32">2. Quis sit fullo, &amp; quid ejus officium?</l>
    <l n="33" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="34" para="true">Distinguitur permutatio à locatione.</l>
    <l n="35">2. An obtinuerit apud Hebraos?</l>
    <l n="36">3. Qua differentia de moribus &amp; jure Ca-</l>
    <l n="37">nonum inter emphyteusin &amp; censum?</l>
    <l n="38">4. Quid moribus &amp; jure Canonum circa</l>
    <l n="39">emphyteusin servetur?</l>
    <l n="40">5. Emphyteuta quid possit?</l>
    <l n="41">6. Quid moribus, &amp; an emphyteusis feu-</l>
    <l n="42">do comparetur?</l>
    <l n="43">7. Differentia inter emphyteusin &amp; loca-</l>
    <l n="44">tionem, &amp; emptionem proponitur.</l>
    <l n="45" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 4. Casus singularis explicatur.</l>
    <l n="46" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="47">1. Ad quid teneatur conductor?</l>
    <l n="48">2. Quid si incendio aedes conflagaverint?</l>
    <l n="49">3. Quid jure Mosaico, &amp; Hebraeorum ob-</l>
    <l n="50">tineat?</l>
    <l n="51" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="52">1. Successor universalis servat locationem</l>
    <l n="53">cum defuncto initam.</l>
    <l n="54">2. Idem non obtinet in successore singulari.</l>
    <l n="55">3. Sunt tamen casus excepti.</l>
    <l n="56">4. Quid variorum moribus obtineat?</l>
    <l n="57" type="heading" level="1" caput="26" para="true">LIBR. 3. TIT. 26.</l>
    <l n="58" type="heading" level="1" caput="26">De Societate.</l>
    <l n="59">1. Quid sit societas?</l>
    <l n="60">2. Varia societatis divisiones circum-</l>
    <l n="61">feruntur.</l>
    <l n="62" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 1. 2. 3.</l>
    <l n="63">1. Qua proportio servanda sit inter socios?</l>
    <l n="64">2. An sortis in societatem collatae sit com-</l>
    <l n="65">munio?</l>
    <l n="66" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="67">1. Unius consensu solvitur societas.</l>
    <l n="68">2. Non tamen ad omnem juris effectum.</l>
    <l n="69" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 5. 7.</l>
    <l n="70" type="foot" para="true">§. 3. 1. Emphyteusis definitur, ejusque natura explicatur.</l>
  </main_text>
